from s5_lib import *
# ---- 9 Application platform services
C(9,"Defender for Containers: what does it cover?","**Posture** (agentless discovery of clusters, misconfiguration recommendations), **vulnerability assessment** of container images in registries and running workloads, and **runtime threat protection** through the **Defender sensor** on nodes plus control-plane audit logs. Works for AKS, and for EKS and GKE through connectors.")
C(9,"AKS access hardening?","Integrate with **Microsoft Entra ID**, use **Azure RBAC for Kubernetes authorization**, and **disable local accounts**. Protect the API server with a **private cluster** or **authorized IP ranges**. Give pods identity with **Microsoft Entra Workload ID**.")
C(9,"AKS workload hardening?","**Network policies** restrict pod-to-pod traffic. **Azure Policy for Kubernetes** audits or denies risky pod settings (privileged containers, host paths). Pull secrets from **Key Vault** with the Secrets Store CSI driver. Keep node images and Kubernetes versions patched.")
C(9,"Azure Container Registry security?","**Disable the admin user**; pull with a **managed identity** and **AcrPull**. **Premium** adds **private endpoints** and more. Restrict public network access, and let Defender for Containers scan images for vulnerabilities.")
C(9,"Securing ACI and Container Apps?","Use **managed identities** instead of stored credentials, deploy into a **virtual network**, keep **secrets** in Key Vault references, and limit **ingress** (Container Apps: internal-only ingress, IP restrictions, built-in authentication).")
C(9,"Azure Functions: authentication and network access?","**Function keys** are shared secrets, fine for simple callers. For real identity use **App Service Authentication (Easy Auth)** with Microsoft Entra ID. Network: **access restrictions**, **private endpoints** (inbound) and **VNet integration** (outbound).")
C(9,"Azure Logic Apps security?","Request triggers are protected by a **SAS signature in the URL**; add **Microsoft Entra OAuth** policies and **IP restrictions**. Turn on **secure inputs and outputs** to hide data in run history. Connect to other services with a **managed identity**.")
C(9,"App Service security settings?","**HTTPS Only**, **minimum TLS version**, **managed identity**, **Key Vault references** for app settings, **built-in authentication**, **access restrictions** and **private endpoints**; turn off FTP and basic-auth publishing.")
C(9,"Azure Web Application Firewall?","Runs on **Application Gateway**, **Front Door** (and Azure CDN). **Managed rule sets** (OWASP-based, bot protection) plus **custom rules** (IP, geo, rate limit). **Detection mode** only logs; **Prevention mode** blocks. Use **exclusions** to fix false positives.")
C(9,"Protecting back-end APIs with API Management?","Policies: **validate-jwt** / validate-azure-ad-token (check tokens), **rate-limit** and **quota** (throttle), **ip-filter**, subscription keys. Authenticate to back ends with a **managed identity** or client certificate. **Defender for APIs** adds inventory, posture and threat detection.")
Q(9,"A new WAF policy on Application Gateway must be tested against production traffic without blocking any requests. Which mode should you use?","Detection",["Prevention","Enforcement","Audit-if-not-exists"],"Detection mode logs matches only. Prevention blocks them.")
Q(9,"Developers currently use a cluster admin certificate to reach AKS. You must make all access go through directory identities and roles. Which TWO should you configure?",["Microsoft Entra integration with Azure RBAC for Kubernetes","Disable local accounts"],["Enable the ACR admin user","Open the API server to all IP addresses"],"Entra plus Azure RBAC gives identity-based access, and disabling local accounts removes the shared admin credential.")
Q(9,"An API in API Management must reject calls that do not carry a valid Microsoft Entra access token with the right audience. Which policy should you add?","validate-jwt",["rate-limit","ip-filter","set-backend-service"],"validate-jwt checks the token's signature, issuer, audience and claims.")
Q(9,"A logic app's run history shows customer passwords passed between actions. What should you turn on?","Secure inputs and outputs on those actions",["Access restrictions on the trigger","A consumption plan","WAF in Detection mode"],"Secure inputs and outputs obfuscate the data in run history.")
Q(9,"An HTTP-triggered function must only accept calls from signed-in users of your tenant. What should you configure?","App Service Authentication with Microsoft Entra ID",["A host key shared with users","A storage account firewall","A function-level key in the URL"],"Keys are shared secrets, not user identity. Built-in authentication validates Entra tokens.")
Q(9,"Defender for Cloud should alert when a container in AKS starts a crypto-mining process. Which component provides that runtime detection?","The Defender sensor deployed by Defender for Containers",["Azure Policy for Kubernetes","The ACR admin user","Network policies"],"The sensor collects runtime signals from nodes for threat detection.")
YN(9,["WAF Prevention mode blocks requests that match rules.","Function keys identify the individual user calling a function.","Premium tier is required for private endpoints on Azure Container Registry."],[1,0,1],"Prevention blocks. Keys are shared secrets. ACR private endpoints need Premium.")
M(9,"Match each service to its key control.",[("AKS pod-to-pod traffic","Network policies"),("ACR image pulls","Managed identity with AcrPull"),("App Service secrets","Key Vault references"),("Throttle API callers","API Management rate-limit policy")],"Segment, authenticate, hide secrets, throttle.")
Q(9,"A WAF managed rule blocks a legitimate form field that contains SQL-like text. What is the best fix?","Add an exclusion for that field",["Switch the whole policy to Detection mode","Delete the managed rule set","Open the back end directly to the internet"],"An exclusion removes the false positive while the rest of the rule set stays on.")
D(9,"Detection mode","Prevention mode","Logs matching requests but lets them through.",0,"Detection only logs.")
D(9,"Function key","App Service Authentication","Validates a Microsoft Entra token for the caller.",1,"Keys are shared secrets.")
D(9,"Network policy","Azure Policy for Kubernetes","Denies pods that run as privileged.",1,"Network policies filter traffic. Azure Policy governs pod specs.")
D(9,"WAF","API Management policies","Blocks SQL injection and cross-site scripting with managed rule sets.",0,"WAF is the OWASP layer.")
# ---- 10 Defender for Cloud posture
C(10,"Foundational CSPM vs Defender CSPM?","**Foundational CSPM (free):** recommendations, secure score, MCSB. **Defender CSPM (paid):** adds **attack path analysis**, **cloud security explorer**, **agentless scanning**, **data security posture** (sensitive data discovery), **governance rules** and risk prioritization.")
C(10,"Attack path analysis and cloud security explorer?","**Attack paths** show chains an attacker could follow from an exposed entry point to a valuable target (for example internet-exposed VM → vulnerable → has permission to a Key Vault). **Cloud security explorer** lets you query the same graph yourself.")
C(10,"Workload protection plans?","Paid plans enabled **per subscription** (some per resource): **Servers, Containers, Storage, Databases, App Service, Key Vault, Resource Manager, APIs, AI Services**. They raise **security alerts**. Turn on with Environment settings or at scale with **Azure Policy**.")
C(10,"Connecting AWS and GCP?","Add a **connector** under Environment settings. **AWS:** deploy the generated **CloudFormation** template (management account or single account). **GCP:** run the generated script in Cloud Shell (organization or project). Servers come in through **Azure Arc**. CSPM is agentless.")
C(10,"Compliance against security frameworks?","The **regulatory compliance dashboard** scores controls for assigned standards across Azure, AWS and GCP. MCSB is default; add standards per subscription or connector, or build **custom standards** and recommendations.")
C(10,"Defender Vulnerability Management for Azure VMs?","The built-in vulnerability scanner for Defender for Servers. **Agent-based** (Defender for Endpoint sensor, P1 and P2) and **agentless** (P2). Findings appear as recommendations with CVEs and software inventory. BYOL scanners are the alternative.")
C(10,"Defender External Attack Surface Management (EASM)?","Maps your **internet-facing assets from the outside**: domains, hosts, IPs, pages, certificates. Starts from **seeds** and discovers connected infrastructure with **no agents or credentials**, exposing unknown and unmanaged ('shadow') assets and their vulnerabilities.")
C(10,"Secure score basics?","A percentage from the MCSB recommendations. Each **control** has a maximum score; you earn it only when **all** its recommendations are fixed for a resource. Exempting a resource removes it from the calculation.")
Q(10,"You need to see how an attacker could move from an internet-exposed VM to a storage account that holds sensitive data. Which capability shows this?","Attack path analysis in Defender CSPM",["Secure score in Foundational CSPM","A workbook in Microsoft Sentinel","Azure Advisor"],"Attack path analysis is a Defender CSPM feature that chains exposures to targets.")
Q(10,"Your company bought another firm. You must find its unknown public websites, hosts and certificates without access to its systems. What should you use?","Defender External Attack Surface Management",["Agentless scanning","Defender for Servers Plan 1","Azure Policy"],"EASM discovers internet-facing assets from the outside using seeds.")
Q(10,"You are connecting an AWS organization to Defender for Cloud. What do you deploy in AWS to create the required roles?","The CloudFormation template generated by the connector wizard",["An Azure Bicep file","A Log Analytics agent on every EC2 instance","A site-to-site VPN"],"The AWS connector produces a CloudFormation template (stack or StackSet).")
Q(10,"Which TWO capabilities require the paid Defender CSPM plan?",["Attack path analysis","Cloud security explorer"],["Secure score","Microsoft cloud security benchmark recommendations"],"Secure score and MCSB recommendations are in free Foundational CSPM.")
YN(10,["Foundational CSPM is free.","Defender workload protection plans produce security alerts.","EASM needs an agent on each discovered asset."],[1,1,0],"Foundational CSPM costs nothing. Plans alert on threats. EASM is agentless and external.")
M(10,"Match each question to the Defender for Cloud feature.",[("How hardened are we overall?","Secure score"),("Do we meet ISO 27001 controls?","Regulatory compliance dashboard"),("Which assets can an attacker chain together?","Attack path analysis"),("What is exposed to the internet that we forgot?","Defender EASM")],"Posture, compliance, paths, outside view.")
Q(10,"You want Defender for Storage and Defender for Servers enabled on every current and future subscription under a management group. What is the best way?","Assign the built-in Azure Policy definitions that configure the Defender plans",["Enable each plan by hand per subscription","Create a budget","Add an AWS connector"],"Policy enables plans at scale and covers new subscriptions.")
Q(10,"Which scanning approach for Azure VM vulnerabilities is available in both Defender for Servers Plan 1 and Plan 2?","Agent-based scanning with the Defender for Endpoint sensor",["Agentless scanning","BYOL only","Packet capture"],"Agentless scanning is Plan 2 only. Agent-based works in both.")
D(10,"Foundational CSPM","Defender CSPM","Includes attack path analysis.",1,"Attack paths are paid CSPM.")
D(10,"CSPM","Workload protection","Raises alerts when an attack is in progress.",1,"CSPM finds misconfigurations. Protection plans detect threats.")
D(10,"Agentless scanning","Defender EASM","Discovers assets from outside with no access to your environment.",1,"EASM is the outside-in view.")
D(10,"Secure score","Regulatory compliance","Driven by the default Microsoft cloud security benchmark recommendations.",0,"Compliance maps to chosen standards.")
# ---- 11 Microsoft Sentinel
C(11,"Workspaces in Microsoft Sentinel?","Sentinel is enabled on a **Log Analytics workspace**. One workspace is simplest; use more for data residency or separate tenants. Onboard the workspace to the **Microsoft Defender portal** for unified incidents; one workspace is **primary**.")
C(11,"Sentinel built-in roles?","**Reader** (view data, incidents, workbooks), **Responder** (Reader + manage incidents), **Contributor** (Responder + create and edit rules, workbooks, install solutions), **Playbook Operator** (list and run playbooks), **Automation Contributor** (for Sentinel's own account to run playbooks from automation rules; **not for users**). Assign at the **resource group**.")
C(11,"Content hub?","Where you install **solutions**: packages of data connectors, analytics rules, workbooks, hunting queries, parsers and playbooks for a product or scenario. Install, then **configure** the connector and enable the rule templates.")
C(11,"Syslog and CEF collection?","Use the **Syslog via AMA** and **Common Event Format via AMA** connectors: a **Linux log forwarder** with the **Azure Monitor Agent** and a **data collection rule**. Syslog lands in the **Syslog** table, CEF in **CommonSecurityLog**.")
C(11,"Windows Security events and WEF?","**Windows Security Events via AMA:** AMA on each machine plus a **DCR** choosing All, Common, Minimal or custom (XPath) events → **SecurityEvent** table. **Windows Forwarded Events:** AMA on a **Windows Event Collector** server that receives events by **WEF** → **WindowsEvent** table.")
C(11,"Custom log tables?","Create a table ending in **_CL** and send data with the **Logs ingestion API** through a **data collection rule** (and endpoint), which can **transform** data with KQL at ingestion. Pick the table's tier: analytics or data lake.")
C(11,"Automation rules vs playbooks?","**Automation rules** run on **incident created, incident updated or alert created**: assign owner, change severity or status, add tags or tasks, suppress, and **run playbooks**, in a set order. **Playbooks** are **Azure Logic Apps** workflows that act on other systems.")
C(11,"Data tiers and retention in Sentinel?","**Analytics tier:** hot data for rules, hunting and workbooks; Sentinel tables keep **90 days** at no extra retention charge, extendable to **2 years**. **Data lake tier:** low-cost storage with **total retention up to 12 years**; no real-time analytics rules; query with KQL jobs and notebooks.")
C(11,"Querying Purview Audit in Defender XDR?","Audit search is available from the **Defender portal** as well as the Purview portal. In **advanced hunting**, Microsoft 365 audit activity is in **CloudAppEvents** (needs the Microsoft 365 app connector in Defender for Cloud Apps). You need audit read permissions.")
Q(11,"A tier-1 analyst must assign and close incidents and run existing playbooks, but must not edit analytics rules. Which TWO roles should you assign?",["Microsoft Sentinel Responder","Microsoft Sentinel Playbook Operator"],["Microsoft Sentinel Contributor","Owner"],"Responder manages incidents, Playbook Operator runs playbooks. Contributor could edit rules.")
Q(11,"Every new high-severity incident must be assigned to the on-call group and trigger a workflow that posts to Teams. What should you create?","An automation rule that sets the owner and runs a playbook",["A workbook","A hunting query","A data collection rule"],"Automation rules react to incident creation and can call playbooks.")
Q(11,"Firewall appliances send logs in Common Event Format. How should you collect them?","A Linux forwarder with Azure Monitor Agent and the CEF via AMA connector",["Install AMA on the firewalls","The Windows Forwarded Events connector","Diagnostic settings on the firewall vendor's portal"],"CEF over Syslog goes through a Linux log forwarder running AMA with a DCR.")
Q(11,"Proxy logs are huge, rarely queried, and must be kept seven years for compliance at the lowest cost. No detections use them. Where should they go?","The data lake tier with long total retention",["The analytics tier with two-year retention","A workbook","An automation rule"],"The data lake tier is the low-cost long-retention option when real-time analytics is not needed.")
Q(11,"Domain controllers already forward events to a Windows Event Collector server. Which connector brings those events into Sentinel?","Windows Forwarded Events",["Common Event Format via AMA","Syslog via AMA","Microsoft Entra ID"],"AMA on the collector reads the forwarded events into the WindowsEvent table.")
YN(11,["Analytics rules can run directly on data stored only in the data lake tier.","Playbooks in Microsoft Sentinel are built on Azure Logic Apps.","Microsoft Sentinel Automation Contributor is intended for analyst user accounts."],[0,1,0],"Lake-only data does not feed real-time rules. Playbooks are Logic Apps. Automation Contributor is for Sentinel's service account.")
M(11,"Match each data source to its table.",[("Linux syslog messages","Syslog"),("Firewall logs in CEF","CommonSecurityLog"),("Windows Security events via AMA","SecurityEvent"),("A custom application log","A table ending in _CL")],"Know where the data lands before you write KQL.")
Q(11,"You need a packaged set of connector, analytics rules and workbooks for a product you just bought. Where do you get it?","Content hub",["Automation rules","The Logs ingestion API","Table management"],"Content hub solutions bundle the content for a product.")
Q(11,"You must drop a noisy field and mask part of another before custom data is stored. Where do you do this?","A KQL transformation in the data collection rule",["An automation rule","A playbook","A workbook parameter"],"DCR transformations change data at ingestion time.")
D(11,"Automation rule","Playbook","A Logic Apps workflow that calls external systems.",1,"Automation rules orchestrate; playbooks act.")
D(11,"Analytics tier","Data lake tier","Supports real-time analytics rules and hunting.",0,"The lake is for cheap, long retention.")
D(11,"Sentinel Responder","Sentinel Contributor","Can create and edit analytics rules.",1,"Responder only manages incidents.")
D(11,"SecurityEvent","WindowsEvent","Receives events collected through Windows Event Forwarding.",1,"WEF data lands in WindowsEvent.")
D(11,"Syslog","CommonSecurityLog","Holds CEF-formatted messages.",1,"CEF is parsed into CommonSecurityLog.")
# ---- 12 Security Copilot
C(12,"What is a Security Compute Unit (SCU)?","The unit of capacity that runs Security Copilot workloads, in the standalone portal, embedded experiences and **agents**. Capacity is an **Azure resource** attached to a **workspace**. Microsoft 365 E5 includes a monthly SCU allowance.")
C(12,"Security Copilot workspaces?","A **workspace** is a scoped, tenant-bound environment where users, plugins, promptbooks and agents operate, with its own **capacity** and role assignments. Auto-provisioned tenants get a **default workspace**.")
C(12,"Security Copilot roles?","**Owner** and **Contributor**. They are **not Entra roles** and give access to the **platform only**, never to security data. **Owners** manage capacity, plugins, role assignment, data sharing and file upload settings. **Contributors** create sessions and use Copilot. At least **two owners** are always kept.")
C(12,"Who gets the roles by default?","Certain Entra roles **inherit Owner** (Global Administrator, Security Administrator and a few others). Contributor defaults to the **Recommended Microsoft Security roles** group; the older **Everyone** default should be removed. Best practice: assign roles to a **security group**.")
C(12,"Why can a Contributor still see no data?","Copilot acts **on behalf of the user**. Each plugin needs the user's own role in that product: for example **Microsoft Sentinel Reader** for the Sentinel plugin, an **Intune** role for Intune. Copilot never goes beyond the user's access.")
C(12,"Plugins?","Connect Copilot to data and tools: **Microsoft** plugins (Defender XDR, Sentinel, Entra, Intune, Purview…), **non-Microsoft** plugins and **custom** plugins. Turn them on under **Manage sources**; some need extra setup. Owners control **who can add and manage custom plugins**.")
C(12,"Agents in Security Copilot?","Agents run tasks with a configured **identity, triggers and permissions**. Find **Microsoft agents** in the agent library and **partner agents** in the **Security Store**; after setup they appear under **Active agents**. Running agents **uses SCUs**. Store subscriptions are billed separately.")
C(12,"Provisioning capacity: who can do it?","You need **Azure Owner or Contributor** on the subscription or resource group (capacity is an Azure resource) and **Security Administrator** or higher in the tenant.")
Q(12,"An analyst has the Security Copilot Contributor role but gets no results when asking about Microsoft Sentinel incidents. What is missing?","A Microsoft Sentinel role such as Microsoft Sentinel Reader",["The Security Copilot Owner role","More security compute units","A custom plugin"],"Copilot roles grant platform access only. Data access comes from the user's role in each product.")
Q(12,"You need to restrict who can upload and use custom plugins in Security Copilot. Which role can change this setting?","Security Copilot Owner",["Security Copilot Contributor","Microsoft Sentinel Contributor","Billing Reader"],"Owners manage plugin settings, capacity and role assignment.")
Q(12,"You want a partner-built agent for phishing triage. Where do you find and acquire it?","Security Store",["Content hub in Sentinel","Azure Marketplace VM images","The Purview portal"],"Partner agents are discovered and bought through the Security Store, then set up in Security Copilot.")
Q(12,"Which TWO are needed to provision Security Copilot capacity?",["Azure Owner or Contributor on the subscription or resource group","Security Administrator or higher in the tenant"],["Microsoft Sentinel Reader","Key Vault Secrets User"],"Capacity is an Azure resource, and onboarding needs a tenant security admin.")
YN(12,["Security Copilot roles are Microsoft Entra roles.","Running an agent consumes security compute units.","Security Copilot can show a user data they have no permission to see in the source product."],[0,1,0],"The roles are Copilot-specific. Agents use SCUs. Copilot works within the user's permissions.")
M(12,"Match each item to its meaning.",[("Unit of Copilot capacity","Security compute unit"),("Connects Copilot to a product's data","Plugin"),("Runs tasks with its own identity and triggers","Agent"),("Scoped environment with its own capacity","Workspace")],"Capacity, connection, automation, scope.")
Q(12,"Security Copilot access is currently given to the Everyone group. You want only security staff to use it, with least effort. What should you do?","Remove Everyone and assign the Recommended Microsoft Security roles group as Contributor",["Make all users Security Administrators","Delete the workspace","Disable all plugins"],"The recommended roles group gives platform access to people who already hold security roles.")
Q(12,"After you get an agent that depends on a plugin, the agent fails. What is the most likely fix?","Configure the dependent plugin under Manage sources",["Buy a second workspace","Assign the agent the Global Administrator role","Turn off audit logging"],"A dependent plugin is enabled with the agent but still needs to be configured.")
D(12,"Copilot Owner","Copilot Contributor","Can manage capacity and assign roles.",0,"Contributors use the platform.")
D(12,"Plugin","Agent","Runs autonomously on a trigger with its own identity.",1,"Plugins connect data sources.")
D(12,"Security Store","Content hub","Where you get partner-built Security Copilot agents.",0,"Content hub is for Sentinel solutions.")
D(12,"Copilot role","Product role (for example Sentinel Reader)","Decides which security data a user can see through Copilot.",1,"Copilot roles only open the platform.")
